# J4 — Bounty operator, scan to finding
# Persona: bug-bounty hunter WITH a key. Workbench → next (phase rail) →
# /full → findings → open <id>. Needs a live model key; skips honestly if
# absent. Point @TARGET at a real fixture repo with KUZUSHI_DEVEX_TARGET.
name: Bounty operator, scan to finding
require-any-env: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY
env: KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TARGET
wait-for: 30 KUZUSHI
snap: workbench-landing
ask: Workbench landing — does the phase chip (組 map 1/4 style) match on-disk reality for a fresh target, or is progress fabricated?
submit: next
wait: 3
snap: phase-rail
ask: `next` — does the phase rail (Map→Hunt→Confirm→Fix) tell the operator what the CURRENT phase needs, with an obvious next action?
submit: /full
wait-live-snap: 30 MAP · ROUTE | guided-map-route
expect: Map establishes the target context Scan engines will consume.
keys: Escape
wait: 1
submit: run sast:scan {}
wait-for: 30 ACTIVITY
snap: scan-running
wait-for: 600 completed
snap: scan-done
keys: Escape
wait: 2
submit: findings
wait: 3
snap: findings-list
ask: Findings — does confidence-first sort hold (Confirmed above Unverified), and is Confirmed-vs-guess visually distinguishable?
submit: open F-0001
wait: 3
snap: finding-detail
ask: Finding detail — is the evidence real and legible, and does the status line honestly reflect triage/verification state?
